    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d682">

                <pb facs="0734" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5741: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-13T12:00:00+08:00">February 13,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 13—5:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Department’s 46, February 11, 1 p.m.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d682-f1"/> In the
                    light of comments made in my 116, February 4, 11 a.m., I recommend that we take
                    no action on this loan other than possibly to ask for a copy of the agreement in
                    view of its possible bearing upon status of Boxer Indemnity payments.<anchor
                        n="89" xml:id="d682-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d682-f1" n="88" xml:id="d682-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d682-f2" n="89" xml:id="d682-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning Boxer Indemnity payments, see <ref target="#pg660"
                        >pp. 660</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
